From: Daniel Ip <kg4368@yahoo.com.hk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow forcing dual-MAC firmware from device tree

ath12k_mhi_register() picks the dual-MAC AMSS firmware (bringing up the
2nd MAC, e.g. the 6 GHz radio of a split-PHY QCN9274) only when the chip's
OTP board_id has the OTP_VALID_DUALMAC_BOARD_ID_MASK bit set.

Some boards run the QCN9274 in dual-MAC mode but leave that OTP bit unset;
the vendor firmware selects the dual-MAC image via its own board config
rather than the OTP. On the Linksys MBE7000 the OTP board_id reads 0x0, so
mainline falls back to the single-MAC image and only 5 GHz comes up (the
2nd MAC fails with "HTC Service WMI MAC1 connect request failed -71").

Allow the device tree to force dual-MAC selection via the
"qcom,ath12k-force-dualmac" property on the wifi node. of_property_read_bool()
is NULL-safe, so non-DT QCN9274 cards are unaffected. The stock QCN9274
firmware-2.bin already carries the AMSS_DUALMAC image and advertises
FW_FEATURE_MLO, so no firmware change is needed.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Ip <kg4368@yahoo.com.hk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/msi.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>

 #include "core.h"
 #include "debug.h"
@@ -344,6 +345,14 @@
 		}
 	}

+	/* Some boards (e.g. Linksys MBE7000) run the QCN9274 in dual-MAC mode
+	 * but leave the OTP dual-MAC board-id bit unset (the vendor selects the
+	 * dual-MAC firmware via its own board config, not the OTP). Let the
+	 * device tree force dual-MAC so the 2nd MAC (e.g. 6 GHz) comes up.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(ab->dev->of_node, "qcom,ath12k-force-dualmac"))
+		dualmac = true;
+
 	if (dualmac) {
 		if (ab->fw.amss_dualmac_data && ab->fw.amss_dualmac_len > 0) {
 			/* use MHI firmware file from firmware-N.bin */
